# Bad inputs fail with guidance and exit code 2.
# REQUIRES: soldb
# RUN: not %soldb run missing.bin 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=MISSING %s
# RUN: not %soldb run 0xzz --runtime 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=MISSING %s
# RUN: not %soldb run %{ethdebug_dir}/TestContract.bin --constructor-args 1 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ABI %s
# RUN: not %soldb run 0x60 --runtime --deploy 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=DEPLOY %s
# RUN: not %soldb run 0x60 --runtime --storage bad 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=STORAGE %s
# A chain the engine cannot model is refused by name before anything runs; one it knows
# only as EVM-equivalent runs, and the summary carries the note.
# RUN: not %soldb run 0x60 --runtime --chain-id 42161 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=CHAIN %s
# RUN: %soldb run 0x6000405060005460010160005500 --runtime --chain-id 10 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOTE %s
# A deployment lands at the CREATE address; `--address` only places `--runtime` code.
# RUN: not %soldb run 0x60 --address 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ADDRESS %s

# MISSING: is not hex bytecode; pass a `.bin` file or a hex string
# ABI: `--constructor-args` need the contract ABI
# DEPLOY: `--deploy` traces creation code
# STORAGE: invalid `--storage` entry `bad`; expected `<slot>=<value>`
# ADDRESS: --runtime
# CHAIN: the replay backend does not model Arbitrum One (chain id 42161)
# CHAIN: --backend debug-rpc
# NOTE: Capability note: OP Mainnet (chain id 10) is replayed with Ethereum mainnet rules
# NOTE: Status: SUCCESS

# A constructor whose arguments are missing reverts, which leaves no code for the call to
# run against. The deployment is checked before the run reports the contract is there, so
# this fails with the reason rather than showing a trace of nothing.
# RUN: %soldb compile %S/../examples/SimpleAuction.sol -o %t.auction.out --solc %{solc_path} > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: not %soldb run %t.auction.out/SimpleAuction.bin "bid()" --value 100 --ethdebug-dir 0x5FbDB2315678afecB367f032d93F642f64180aa3:SimpleAuction:%t.auction.out 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=CONSTRUCTOR %s

# CONSTRUCTOR: the contract was not deployed
# CONSTRUCTOR: pass the constructor's arguments with `--constructor-args`
